{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "4e0090ca-ae80-87b5-aca1-8feb6e67cc7d",
  "created_at": "2025-12-20T11:16:11-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Patrick Reardon",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:15-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Lorraine. I know it's Saturday, so you've reached the weekend line. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:23-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Lorraine. Yes, thank you. My name is Patrick Reardon. I am calling on the storm line because City Hall is closed today, no? I understand this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:32-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right, the office is closed on weekends, but this line gets checked. What's going on, Mr. Reardon?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:38-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The water. From the soaker that ended Thursday, two days ago, it is still sitting. At the low spot at the end of my block, on Kingston Avenue, there is about a foot of water. A foot. Two days, and it does not go down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:52-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A foot of water, still there from Thursday. And what's the address you're nearest to?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:14:58-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Two sixty-eight Kingston Avenue. I have my business there, and the low spot is at the end of the block, by the corner. Ai, meu Deus. It is the same every time it rains hard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:09-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, two sixty-eight Kingston Avenue, low spot at the end of the block, about a foot deep. Do you know if the drain is blocked?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:17-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I cannot say. Maybe leaves, maybe something else. I only see the water, no drain. And it is Saturday, so children are out, they walk through, they play. People with dogs also, they go right near the edge. I worry somebody slips, or a child goes in. It is not a small puddle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:34-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I'll put this in as a standing-water hazard so the crew sees it today. Can I confirm a number to call you back on? I have 401-555-0151."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:43-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is correct. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-five-one. Please, when it is done, when they have fixed it, you call me back. I would like to know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:52-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Will do. I'll note that you want a call once the work is finished. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:15:58-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that is all. I am putting my scarf around my neck now and going outside, I will keep watching it. Thank you, Lorraine. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-20T11:16:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too, Mr. Reardon. Stay clear of that water. Bye now."
    }
  ],
